          roughly $400 more but buys a genuinely stronger 3.5 CHP motor, two
          extra inches of deck width, and 50 more pounds of weight capacity
          — worth it the moment running becomes a regular habit rather than
          an occasional activity. Against NordicTrack's budget T Series, the
          F63 costs more but delivers a noticeably heavier frame, a larger
          deck, and Sole's stronger warranty terms; the T Series undercuts it
          on price but with a lighter-duty build that shows up more quickly
          under regular use.
